00:10:36.196 --> 00:10:38.156
and how would you recommend a prep for it

00:10:38.156 --> 00:10:41.146
either on Khan Academy
or off of Khan Academy?

00:10:41.146 --> 00:10:42.696
- Great question.

00:10:42.696 --> 00:10:44.126
The essay is optional,

00:10:44.126 --> 00:10:46.649
but as many things are in life,

00:10:48.466 --> 00:10:50.936
those things that are maybe recommended

00:10:50.936 --> 00:10:54.076
are things that are that
many colleges like to see

00:10:54.076 --> 00:10:58.076
and I have heard that if
colleges really want to get

00:10:58.076 --> 00:11:01.536
an authentic piece of a
writing sample from somebody,

00:11:01.536 --> 00:11:05.966
they are able to actually
see your essay from the SAT

00:11:05.966 --> 00:11:08.786
because colleges know that if you write,

00:11:08.786 --> 00:11:12.103
if you submit an essay as part
of your college application,

00:11:12.103 --> 00:11:14.066
you may have had help.

00:11:14.066 --> 00:11:17.636
So if they're wondering that
something doesn't add up,

00:11:17.636 --> 00:11:19.636
they might actually look
at your copy of your essay.

00:11:19.636 --> 00:11:22.566
So if you feel like it
could be a strong component

00:11:22.566 --> 00:11:26.536
of your overall profile,
I'd say, definitely take it

00:11:26.536 --> 00:11:29.016
and I know that many colleges

00:11:29.016 --> 00:11:30.566
do encourage people to take it,

00:11:31.726 --> 00:11:35.386
as for preparation it
is definitely important

00:11:35.386 --> 00:11:39.776
to understand that the SAT essay topic

00:11:39.776 --> 00:11:44.276
is a lot like a writing assignment
you might get in college.

00:11:44.276 --> 00:11:46.446
So preparing for the SAT

00:11:46.446 --> 00:11:48.496
is a process of preparing

00:11:48.496 --> 00:11:52.246
to become a more effective
writer in college.

00:11:52.246 --> 00:11:54.116
